<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Addition law for mutually exclusive events</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>Learners at a school in [[if test="is(town=0)"]]Machakos[[elif test="is(town=1)"]]Kitui[[else]]Embu[[/if]] each travel to school in one way only. A learner is chosen at random. The table shows the probabilities. The probability for bicycle is missing.</p><table border="1" style="border-collapse:collapse;text-align:center;"><tr><th style="padding:4px 10px;">Way of travelling</th><th style="padding:4px 10px;">Walk</th><th style="padding:4px 10px;">Matatu</th><th style="padding:4px 10px;">Boda boda</th><th style="padding:4px 10px;">Bicycle</th></tr><tr><td style="padding:4px 10px;">Probability</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@pdec(p1)@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@pdec(p2)@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@pdec(p3)@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">&nbsp;</td></tr></table><p>Give each probability exactly, as a fraction or an exact decimal.</p><p>(a) Find \(P(\text{bicycle})\).</p><div>[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div><p>(b) Find \(P(\text{walks or travels by boda boda})\).</p><div>[[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div><p>(c) Find \(P(\text{does not travel by matatu})\).</p><div>[[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>Each learner travels in exactly one way, so the four ways are mutually exclusive and their probabilities add to 1.</p><p>(a) \(P(\text{bicycle}) = 1 - ({@pdec(p1)@} + {@pdec(p2)@} + {@pdec(p3)@}) = {@pdec(ta1)@}\).</p><p>(b) A learner cannot both walk and take a boda boda, so add: \({@pdec(p1)@} + {@pdec(p3)@} = {@pdec(ta2)@}\).</p><p>(c) The complement: \(P(\text{not matatu}) = 1 - {@pdec(p2)@} = {@pdec(ta3)@}\). As a check, walk, boda boda and bicycle together give \({@pdec(p1)@} + {@pdec(p3)@} + {@pdec(ta1)@} = {@pdec(ta3)@}\).</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>3</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026063000</text></stackversion>
  <questionvariables>
    <text><![CDATA[/* pdec: exact decimal display of a value with at most 4 decimal places */
pdec(v) := if integerp(v) then v elseif integerp(10*v) then dispdp(float(v),1) elseif integerp(100*v) then dispdp(float(v),2) elseif integerp(1000*v) then dispdp(float(v),3) else dispdp(float(v),4);
/* Design: ways of travelling to school are mutually exclusive outcomes of one choice. Entries in hundredths [walk, matatu, boda boda]. Source: original. */
L: [[17,30,28],[15,33,36],[17,35,26],[30,34,9],[42,16,27],[11,28,44],[29,18,34],[35,28,17],[29,18,27],[39,19,12]];
ix: 1+rand(10);
p1: L[ix][1]/100; p2: L[ix][2]/100; p3: L[ix][3]/100;
town: mod(ix,3);
ta1: 1-p1-p2-p3; ta2: p1+p3; ta3: 1-p2;
tl1: min(1/200,ta1/20); tl2: min(1/200,ta2/20); tl3: min(1/200,ta3/20);
/* diagnostics */
miss1: 1-p1-p2;
mult2: p1*p3;
just3: p2;
part3: p1+p3;]]></text>
  </questionvariables>
